Database migrations (Alembic, via Flask-Migrate)

- Build a fresh database with `flask db upgrade`.
- The test suite builds its schema with db.create_all(), not this chain.
- The baseline's id is `0001_v2`, not `0001`, so a 1.x database at its own
  revision `0001` is never mistaken for it.
- New revisions should use an explicit sequential id, the next number after
  the latest file in versions/ (e.g. `0002`):
  `flask db migrate --rev-id 0002 -m "..."`.
- New revisions are formatted with ruff as they're written (see alembic.ini).
